      "category": "security",
      "title": "Provider credential is reachable in Git history",
      "message": "A credential-shaped value added in commit fdfa32a is still reachable in Git history. The value was withheld.",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/demo/fixture.ts"
      },
      "evidence": [
        {
          "type": "file",
          "path": "src/demo/fixture.ts",
          "detail": "commit fdfa32a; detector github-classic; 1 added-line occurrence(s); value withheld."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "A credential remains reachable to anyone with repository history access even after it is deleted from the working tree.",
      "remediationConstraints": [
        "Rotate or revoke the credential first; history rewriting cannot un-expose it.",
        "Use the repository's authorized history-rewriting workflow outside Codebase Doctor.",
        "Coordinate with collaborators before rewriting shared history."
      ],
      "remediation": "Have an authorized human or external coding agent rotate or revoke the credential, remove it from history with an authorized tool, then rerun a full audit.",
      "verification": {
